Build JSON arrays and objects in linear time.

ToJsonList/ToJsonMap fold with std::accumulate over an init value of type
nlohmann::json while the lambda takes nlohmann::json::array_t (object_t) by
value. Every step converts the accumulated basic_json&& into array_t through
get<array_t>(), a deep copy of everything serialized so far, so serializing
n table-metadata snapshots costs n(n+1)/2 snapshot-object copies. GlamDB writes
a new root with every append: at 2000 retained snapshots one 1-row append spent
3.6 s in this serialization (TableMetadataUtil::Write: 3449 ms for a 1.77 MB
root; doubling n quadrupled the time).

